{"id":"gen-1794526722-F42hs16t9StHBT8kQkzC","object":"chat.completion","created":1794526722,"model":"meta/muse-ember","provider":"Meta","system_fingerprint":null,"service_tier":"default","choices":[{"index":0,"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop","native_finish_reason":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{
  "rating": 0.40,
  "explanation": "Combined regime pairs national document, federal-facility, entry-fraud and custody exposures with a narrower, unenforced state school/college facility law. A visitor with matching home documents and private services faces mainly friction and age-dependent school/care uncertainty, but discrepancy at entry can lead to refusal, investigation, detention under documented abusive birth-sex/conversion practices, or hormone interruption. Courts have enjoined some measures, hate-crime and employment protections exist nationally, and private/public-accommodation discrimination is barred only in some municipalities. Unremedied universal document/facility rules and severe custody terms place this below the 0.45 profile, while absence of organised police targeting, a criminal bathroom penalty in this state, or a state-wide private-facility ban keeps it above 0.35.",
  "factor_matrix": {
    "entry_documents": {
      "exposure": "National binary passport policy stopped new X or non-birth-sex markers in Feb 2025; Supreme Court allowed it Nov 2025. Entry cable directs refusal and more evidence where documents/records create reasonable sex doubt, with possible lifetime fraud ineligibility for wilful material misrepresentation; passports reportedly blocked/confiscated.",
      "protection": "Existing X passports remain valid to expiration. Fraud finding requires four elements, is not automatic, and has limited waivers; passport policy is under civil-liberties litigation.",
      "interaction": "Document discrepancy can trigger refusal, investigation and custody, converting a border issue into detention and birth-sex placement exposure.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "investigation_detention_custody": {
      "exposure": "From 2026 national corrections adopted conversion-therapy model: short hair, hormone removal, psychiatric substitution. Immigration custody reports for trans men include forced labour, beatings, solitary and severe sexual abuse, with guards using gendered justification.",
      "protection": "Some national orders have been blocked or are litigated, but dossier does not document an operative remedy changing the adopted custody practices. Not documented.",
      "interaction": "Entry, facility or fraud investigation leading to detention exposes the traveller to the documented custody regime, including medication denial.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "federal_state_facilities": {
      "exposure": "National order bars government-funded single-sex facilities inconsistent with birth sex. This state's 2024/2025 law requires public and private K-12 and colleges to designate bathrooms, locker/changing/shower rooms and overnight accommodation by birth certificate.",
      "protection": "Single-occupancy restrooms are exempt. State law has no criminal penalty or enforcement mechanism and no documented arrest or citation; most non-educational private settings are not covered by this state law.",
      "interaction": "Federal facilities create nationwide exposure; the state law mainly affects minors, students and overnight educational accommodation rather than ordinary adult visitors.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "care_services": {
      "exposure": "State minor care/sports bill bans puberty blockers, hormones and surgery under 18, but was re-enjoined Mar 2025; operative status unresolved. Custody hormone removal is documented. National minor-care executive action and proposed insurance rules are contested.",
      "protection": "Re-enjunction and abandonment of Jan 2024 adult-care proposal mean no documented current adult-care ban. Emergency-care practice for visitors is not documented.",
      "interaction": "A minor needing care, medication continuity or emergency admission faces uncertain state law plus national funding/hostility measures; detention can interrupt hormones.",
      "status": "uncertain"
    },
    "threat_framing_law_enforcement": {
      "exposure": "Official measures frame gender identity as ideology, direct school investigations and possible teacher prosecution for facilitating social transition, and 2026 counterterrorism strategy prioritises groups described as radically pro-transgender. Polling records 66% support for birth-sex document listing.",
      "protection": "Several orders are blocked/enjoined and courts remain active; national hate-crime law covers gender identity. Dossier does not document organised police sweeps or extortion in this state.",
      "interaction": "State threat-framing increases scrutiny at schools, borders and agencies, while litigation creates variable real-world enforcement.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "minors_guardians": {
      "exposure": "Minor students must use facilities matching birth certificate, including overnight accommodation. Jan 2025 law requires staff to out LGBTQ students to parents. Care and sports bans are enacted but re-enjoined, status uncertain; national order threatens teachers using preferred names/pronouns.",
      "protection": "Single-occupancy exemption and current injunction of care/sports provisions reduce immediate exposure, but guardian rights and school practice are not documented.",
      "interaction": "A travelling minor enrolled or housed through an educational institution faces facility, outing and care uncertainty that an adult alone ordinarily does not.",
      "status": "uncertain"
    },
    "street_violence_police_response": {
      "exposure": "No state-specific pattern of street attacks or police targeting of visitors is documented. Public support for birth-sex documents is noted, but underlying incidents and rates are not documented.",
      "protection": "Gender-identity hate crimes are punishable nationally; state has no gender-identity anti-discrimination statute in private employment, housing or public accommodations, though 33 municipalities have ordinances and a 2018 state executive order covers state employment.",
      "interaction": "Patchy local ordinances and absent state statute make recourse location-dependent if harassment occurs in visitor-facing services.",
      "status": "not_documented"
    },
    "remedies_unknowns": {
      "exposure": "July 2026 assessment places state in second-highest tier among 16, based on statutory text/litigation, not measured incidents. Several national and state measures are enjoined or unresolved, including care/sports, adult-care replacement and Aug 2026 vehicle-marker rules.",
      "protection": "Courts have blocked or enjoined several orders, ACLU litigation challenges passports, and municipal ordinances provide partial remedies. Other orders remain in effect, including allowed passport restriction.",
      "interaction": "Traveller cannot reliably assume either full enforcement or full injunction; checking operative status before travel is essential, but uncertainty itself is exposure.",
      "status": "uncertain"
    }
  },
