  "synthesis": "The operative interaction is document or presentation discrepancy at entry or in a government/educational facility, followed by possible refusal, investigation, detention, birth-sex placement and interruption of hormones. Litigation and local ordinances mitigate some measures, and this state's education law lacks penalties, but they do not cancel the allowed national passport rule, federal facility restriction, uncertain minor-care status, or custody practices. For an adult using private services with consistent documents, daily exposure is substantially lower than the custody/entry worst case; for a minor in education or anyone detained, exposure is much higher."
